---
# The hosting layer under the {{ tenant }} platform hosts: what a provider
# would otherwise supply. A hypervisor, a backup server for its guests, and an
# ingress VM that shares one public address between the tenant VMs. Not part
# of the operations platform (§ 7 PLX): provision.yml and configure.yml bind
# apps to hosts; this playbook makes those hosts exist, reachable and
# restorable.
#
#   mise hosting
#
# The inventory groups it expects (inventory/hosts.yml): proxmox, pbs, haproxy,
# and guests for every VM on the hypervisor, the ingress VM included.
# A fresh host is reached as root once and joins the overlay network with a
# use-once setup key from the environment:
#
#   NETBIRD_SETUP_KEY=… mise hosting -- --limit <host> -u root -e ansible_host=<public name>
#
# A new guest takes two runs: the first creates it from configure_guests_list
# on the hypervisor, the second reaches it as the first admin on the address
# it was given and joins it to the overlay. A guest without a public address
# is reached through the ingress VM. The guest refuses the login until its
# first boot has created the admin, a minute or so after the first run:
#
#   mise hosting -- --limit <hypervisor>
#   NETBIRD_SETUP_KEY=… mise hosting -- --limit <guest> -u <first admin> \
#     -e ansible_host=<address> \
#     -e ansible_ssh_common_args='-oProxyJump=<ingress VM> -oStrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new'
#
- name: Host baseline of the hosting layer
  hosts: proxmox:pbs:haproxy
  become: true
  roles:
    - plexus.platform.configure_base
    - plexus.platform.configure_hostname
    - plexus.platform.install_and_join_netbird
    - plexus.platform.configure_iam
    - plexus.platform.configure_unattended_upgrades
    - plexus.platform.configure_mail # does nothing until configure_mail_smtp is set

- name: Configure the hypervisor
  hosts: proxmox
  become: true
  roles:
    - plexus.platform.configure_proxmox # web UI on the overlay, firewall, storage, guest bridge, backup jobs
    - plexus.platform.configure_guests  # creates the VMs the other plays and playbooks configure

# The firewall first: Proxmox Backup Server listens on every address, and
# configure_pbs refuses to install it on a host whose firewall is not loaded.
- name: Configure the backup server
  hosts: pbs
  become: true
  roles:
    - plexus.platform.configure_firewall
    - plexus.platform.configure_pbs # datastore, retention, the clients that may push to it

- name: Configure the ingress VM
  hosts: haproxy
  become: true
  roles:
    - plexus.platform.configure_haproxy  # SNI/Host routing to the tenant VMs, NAT for the guest bridge
    - plexus.platform.configure_firewall # after the role that adds rules to it

# Every VM on the hypervisor, whichever platform runs on it: what the hosting
# layer itself needs from a guest. The agent lets a backup freeze the file
# systems; the overlay is how the guest is reached from then on.
- name: Guests of the hypervisor
  hosts: guests
  become: true
  pre_tasks:
    # A new guest upgrades its packages on first boot and holds apt meanwhile.
    - name: Wait for the first boot to finish
      ansible.builtin.command:
        cmd: cloud-init status --wait
      changed_when: false
      failed_when: false
  roles:
    - plexus.platform.configure_base
    - plexus.platform.install_qemu_guest_agent
    - plexus.platform.install_and_join_netbird

# Last: closes root logins once an admin has logged in.
- name: Key-only SSH on the hosting layer's hosts
  hosts: proxmox:pbs:haproxy
  become: true
  roles:
    - plexus.platform.configure_sshd
